mt7915: CR6608 uplink trigger-based attribution accounting v2

Corrects three defects in the patch-07 host accounting that the on-device
evidence verdicts depend on, plus two guards, and adds machine-readable
firmware statistics:

1. he_tb_ppdu / he_tb_full_bw / he_tb_ul_ofdma_ru counted RX descriptors
   (MPDUs of an A-MPDU and hardware-deaggregated A-MSDU subframes), not
   PPDUs.  They are now deduplicated per (peer, RXD group-2 PHY start
   time); the raw descriptor count is kept as he_tb_mpdu.

2. Full-bandwidth UL MU-MIMO credit (he_tb_ul_mumimo_shared) went only to
   the peer whose frame completed the two-peer group, so with two clients
   the "two credited peers" verdict depended on delivery order.  Every peer
   of a recognised group is now credited (the first by WCID lookup under
   the NAPI RCU read side; third/fourth full-bandwidth users as they join).

3. QoS-Null responses to the firmware's BSR polls (BSRP triggers) were
   counted like data, so two idle peers could satisfy a multi-user verdict
   with no uplink data.  Frames are now split by frame control into
   he_tb_data_ppdu / he_tb_nulldata_ppdu / he_tb_fc_unknown, and
   ul_{ofdma,mumimo}_multi_user_data_ppdus count a group only once two
   distinct peers have each contributed a data-bearing frame.

Guards: a descriptor without RXD group 2 (no PHY start time) is counted as
he_tb_no_timestamp and never absorbed into a stale group; a frame with a
failed FCS is ignored (its WCID is not trustworthy).

muru_stats additionally prints one key=value line per firmware counter
(dl_he_*, ul_hetrig_*) with an explicit source/semantics footer: the
MURU_GET_TXC_TX_STATS counters are the firmware's TX-command-side trigger
accounting bucketed by solicited allocation; whether a bucket increments on
trigger transmission or on TB reception is not determinable from
host-visible source.  Both debugfs nodes now carry schema=2.

Cost: confined to MT_PHY_TYPE_HE_TB frames while an uplink bit is armed
and RXD group 5 is enabled, i.e. evidence windows.  Read-only telemetry.

